\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE-Dlr/yen regains balance, euro subdued. \b0\par\par\uc2 815 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 1999\par 13:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 12 (Reuters) - The yen took a slight breather at Europe's midsession on Tuesday after being beaten down against the dollar and euro earlier on apparent dollar/yen buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But traders said the yen's calm right now belied the market's mood, which was nervous as traders looked for further signs of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  They were also gearing up for the opening of the U.S. session, bracing for further dollar buying to cover short positions, or for selling to take profits on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rebound of more than four percent from Monday's 28-month low. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone's still quite jumpy but dollar/yen seems to have stabilised above 112 yen for now at least. The same goes for euro/yen. Now people are waiting to see what the U.S. market will do," said one trader at a Japanese bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "No-one really expects the Fed to follow (and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), but we're waiting for any comments from the U.S. authorities." \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen surged back up by more than four yen, or nearly four percent, on Tuesday after traders said the BOJ appeared to be buying dollars, first below 110 yen and then around 111. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar's gains on Tuesday were on a scale unseen since the Japanese and U.S. central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly in August 1995 to push dollar/yen higher. \par \par \uc2  However, there was widespread doubt as to whether the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could get much mileage out of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We have seen in the past that independent rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  don't have a lasting impact, and markets are still sceptical about how long it can last," said Michael Lewis, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Deutsche Bank. \par \par \uc2  "The picture will change only if the Federal Reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the dollar. But that's unlikely." \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 112.43/53 yen at 1200 GMT, off its earlier session high of 112.80 but well above the low of 108.17 seen on Monday which was its weakest since September 1996. \par \par \uc2  So far, Japanese authorities have declined to comment on any dollar buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said he had received no report on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the Japanese have issued more aggressive verbal warnings to yen bulls, who have driven dollar/yen down by about 13 percent since the beginning of December. Traders and analysts attribute much of the yen's gains to investors' eagerness to buy Japanese government bonds, whose yields have rocketed in the past month. \par \par \uc2  Despite a warning from Japan's top government spokesman Hiromu Nonaka on Tuesday that an excessively strong yen was not good for the global economy, analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength to continue. \par \par \uc2  "It's still not obvious whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be sufficient to change the yen's trend right now," said Jane Foley, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Capital. \par \par \uc2  "Japan's long-term interest rates are rising. While the Japanese authorities have now signalled they are unhappy with dollar/yen below 110, it's unlikely it will rebound very strongly," she said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts were also looking at the dollar side of the equation. The market will keep an anxious eye on developments in Latin America - a crucial trading partner for the United States - after a Brazilian state declared a moratorium on its debt payments to the central government last week. \par \par \uc2  While euro/yen was moving largely because of the skirmishes in dollar/yen, Europe's new single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed to be losing a bit of shine of its own accord as the market pondered the economic basics of the euro-zone. \par \par \uc2  "It looks like the European economies are weaker than that of the U.S.," said Deutsche's Lewis. "It's likely there will be a rate cut in Europe next month, and there is very quiet talk that there may be a rate hike in the U.S.. So the interest rate factor is working in favour of the dollar." \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday the euro fell to $1.1440, its weakest since its market launch on January 4. It was last at $1.1497/05, down 3.5 percent from the $1.1906 peak seen on the day of its debut. \par \par \uc2  Data on Tuesday confirmed the market's view of subdued European economies. \par \par \uc2  The Reuters Eurozone Purchasing Managers' Index showed manufacturing in the euro zone slipped in December, with the index at 46.9 compared with 47.2 in November. \par \par \uc2  Separately, German industrial output decreased by 2.3 percent month-on-month in November after a rise of 1.4 percent in October. \par \par \uc2  ((Chizu Nomiyama, London newsroom 44 171 542 6721, chizu.nomiyama@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1c06vxa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
