\par\par \b \uc2  JGBs down by midday as stocks recover on yen fall. \b0\par\par\uc2 613 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 1999\par 04:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 12 (Reuters) - Japanese government bond (JGB) futures and cash bond prices were weaker by midday on Tuesday after the yen's sharp fall against the dollar prompted a recovery in Tokyo stocks. \par \par \uc2  The yield of the key 203rd 1.800 percent 10-year JGB was at 1.785 percent at 0222 GMT, against Monday's close of 1.750 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The yen's fall and strong stocks mean selling of JGBs," said a trader at a major Japanese brokerage house. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, some investors continued unloading long-term JGBs to make room for a fresh supply of six-year JGBs offered in an auction on Tuesday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) said earlier on Tuesday that it was offering 900 billion yen in 1.5 percent six-year JGBs through a price-competitive auction. \par \par \uc2  The offering volume and coupon rate were both in line with expectations, traders said. The auction will close at noon (0300 GMT) and the results are due at 0530 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The brokerage house trader said selling was detected in the newly auctioned 209th 2.0 percent 10-year JGB. \par \par \uc2  The bond's yield rose to around 1.850 percent by late morning trade, compared with Monday's finish of around 1.800 percent. \par \par \uc2  The key Nikkei stock average ended the morning at 13,477.77, up 109.29 points or 0.82 percent from Monday's close, supported by a rise in share prices of Japanese export-driven manufacturers. \par \par \uc2  The index had briefly dipped as low as 13,212.30, weighed down by the dollar's fall to a 28-month low near 108.21 yen overnight. \par \par \uc2  The dollar surged above 111 yen by late morning trade after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's apparent dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Key March 10-year JGB futures ended the morning at 130.13, down 0.35 from Monday's close. Turnover was 20,217 contracts. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the six-year JGB auction is likely to attract sound bids, led by brokerage houses. \par \par \uc2  "Some banks may buy. But major bidders seem to be brokerages because many of them want to increase holdings in the medium-term zone," said a senior trader at another major brokerage house. \par \par \uc2  Given the likely upward trend in bond yields due to an increased supply of government debt, investment is less risky in medium-term JGBs than in long-term JGBs, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Also, Japanese banks are reluctant to buy long-term JGBs after many suffered capital losses when the bubble of inflated bond prices burst in December, they said. \par \par \uc2  Last year, banks sought quality and liquidity and put too much weight on 10-year JGBs, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said there was uncertainty over what Japanese life insurers, many of which have invested in foreign assets in the past few months, would do if the dollar resumed a downward trend against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "If their portfolios are hurt, that may result in their repatriation of funds from foreign investment. That could flow into JGBs. But if their business is seriously hurt, concerns over the Japanese financial system may resurface," said a manager at a domestic brokerage house. \par \par \uc2  Key June three-month euroyen futures firmed on short-covering after the dollar snapped back above 111 yen. \par \par \uc2  June ended the morning at 99.43, up 0.05 from Monday's settlement. Turnover was 20,117 contracts. \par \par \uc2  The key overnight call rate firmed to around 0.23 percent from Monday's weighted average of 0.21 percent. ((Risa Maeda, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-3432-8570 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1c06viy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
