\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr gains strongly in Tokyo on apparent BOJ action. \b0\par\par\uc2 721 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 1999\par 08:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 12 (Reuters) - The dollar was sharply higher against the yen in late afternoon on Tuesday in Tokyo, after apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) to halt the yen's appreciation, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  BOJ dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , apparently the first of its kind since August 1995, drove the dollar up by more than three yen from its earlier Tokyo low. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 111.35/45 yen as of 0614 GMT, compared with 108.60/65 yen in New York late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit briefly rose as high as 111.85 yen in early afternoon from an earlier Tokyo low of 108.65 yen. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ was likely to have placed dollar bids at several commercial banks that are among eligible agent banks for its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including two major U.S. investment banks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A senior official at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) who is in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  "With today's BOJ action, monetary authorities have shown a clear determination that they would not tolerate the dollar's fall below 110 yen," said a dealer at a Japanese bank. "So the dollar's downside could remain solid, at least in the near term. \par \par \uc2  Dollar purchases against the yen in Tokyo on Tuesday by the BOJ may have totalled as much as $1 billion, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa told a news conference earlier on Tuesday that he was watching recent movements in the yen closely, but he declined to comment on the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, saying he left that up to specialists within the ministry. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar was lifted from lows as aggressive dollar buying by a U.S. financial institution prompted talk that the BOJ was checking on dollar/yen rates. \par \par \uc2  The dollar extended gains in late morning, as the BOJ apparently stepped in to buy dollars starting from levels below 110 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar surged above 111 yen as a wave of stop-loss dollar buying was triggered between 110.10 and 110.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed to have continued to buy dollars above 111 yen. \par \par \uc2  There was also talk that the BOJ might have been behind the dollar's brief spike to 111.85 yen in early afternoon. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's upside was capped by heavy offers, including those from Japanese investors and exporters. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of Japanese investors are under-hedged as the pace of the dollar's recent drop was so fast," said a dealer at a trust bank. "So there are likely to be significant dollar offers from Japanese players between 112 and 115 yen." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar was still vulnerable due to concerns over Brazil's financial situation and to increased U.S-Japan trade friction. \par \par \uc2  "The balance of demand and supply of dollars against the yen has clearly changed since the end of last year," Shinji Yamada, senior manager of international treasury at Fuji Bank, told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  "The net surplus that Japan has in its current account is clearly making the dollar/yen heavy on the topside. So in the due course, the natural movement will tend to be for the dollar to move downside," Yamada added. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the market would still remain cautious about selling dollars too aggressively in the near term as the BOJ was likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again. \par \par \uc2  "I think the BOJ will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again at below 110 yen, and I think they should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Kazuo Takayama chief manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at Midland Bank in Tokyo, told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  The dollar later extended gains on talk of more BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late Tokyo trade. The dollar briefly rose as high as 112.65 yen, up four yen from an earlier Tokyo low. \par \par \uc2  Reported comments by Japan's Chief Cabinet Secretary Hiromu Nonaka also helped to lift the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Nonaka was quoted by Jiji news agency on Tuesday as saying that an excessive yen rise was not desirable for the world economy. ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1c06r7v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
