\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes \highlight\uc2  to check strong yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 698 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 1999\par 10:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 12 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan (BOJ) showed its determination to check the yen's surge against the dollar on Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time since August 1995, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move, although giving the dollar some temporary relief, was not expected to halt its bearish trend for long. \par \par \uc2  Rumours of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which bankers said may have totalled $1 billion or more in the morning alone, sparked heavy short-covering of the dollar from a low of 108.65 yen in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "It (the BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the right time today and it should continue doing that if the dollar falls below 110 yen again," Kazuo Takayama, chief manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at Midland Bank, said in an interview with Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is seen moving in a range between 110 and 115 yen now, with caution over the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to grow strongly below 110," he added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar climbed over four yen to 112.85 yen from the day's low as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to buy dollars intermittently from around 111 yen in late afternoon trade, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  As of 0900 GMT, the dollar stood at 112.50/60 yen. \par \par \uc2  Overnight in New York, the dollar fell to a 28-month low of 108.21 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market remained more sensitive to yen-buying factors, such as rises in Japanese government bond (JGB) yields and pessimism over Wall Street's outlook, than to dollar-buying incentives. \par \par \uc2  Jitters over the situation in Brazil and worries about the outlook of the U.S. economy were also depressing the dollar's underlying sentiment, particularly against the yen, they said. \par \par \uc2  "It's still more likely that the basic yen-buying trend will persist," said Mitsuru Saito, chief economist of the Treasury section at Sanwa Bank. \par \par \uc2  "Given the recent rallies in JGB yields there is still strong demand by foreign investors to buy the yen, which should keep the yen supported," Saito said. \par \par \uc2  In the near term, the market was likely to sit back and assess how determined the BOJ is to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ was thought to have reacted to this by buying dollars for yen, starting from levels below 110 yen in morning Tokyo trade. \par \par \uc2  A senior official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on the possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  But banking sources said the BOJ was first rumoured to have checked the dollar/yen rate at around the low of 108.65 yen and then later bought dollars at levels below 110 yen. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to have placed dollar bids at several commercial banks that are among eligible agent banks for the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including two major U.S. investment banks. \par \par \uc2  Comments by Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa also spurred speculation that the BOJ could be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  secretly. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa declined to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying he "left that up to the specialists within the ministry". \par \par \uc2  Chief Cabinet Secretary Hiromu Nonaka also weighed in later in the day, saying that an excessive rise in the yen was not desirable for the world economy, according to the Jiji news agency. \par \par \uc2  Nonaka's comments also fuelled yen sales, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Shinji Yamada, senior manager of international treasury at Fuji Bank, said Tokyo authorities might be trying to keep any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  quiet as it might be seen as contradicting their widely publicised efforts to promote the yen. \par \par \uc2  "It seems there is some kind of dilemma among Japanese monetary authorities. They are trying to internationalise the yen, encouraging foreign investors to buy yen assets. For that, it would not be wise to tell the world the upside of the yen is limited from here," Yamada told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  "I would not be surprised if they (the authorities) would not like to show that they are in the market." ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1c06r43\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
