\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr ends U.S. mixed after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  boost. \b0\par\par\uc2 626 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 1999\par 23:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Jan 12 (Reuters) - The dollar closed New York trading firmer against the yen as Japanese officials tried to curb the unit's recent gains, but it fell against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid fears of an imminent Latin American crisis. \par \par \uc2  After days of speculation about how Tokyo may choose to tackle the yen's recent strength, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers reported that the Bank of Japan bought dollars for yen below 110 yen and helped send the dollar over four yen higher overnight. \par \par \uc2  But dealers admitted the gains would likely be short-lived as the market is ready to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's will in pushing the yen lower. \par \par \uc2  "One \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not change the fact that there is not a great deal of demand for dollars right now, and in a number of days I expect the dollar to be lower again," predicted John McCarthy, senior vice president at ING Barings Capital. \par \par \uc2  While Japan's top financial diplomat Eisuke Sakakibara, known in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at Mr. Yen for his ability to move markets, also spoke out against an excessively strong yen, the markets seemed to listen less at the end of the day. \par \par \uc2  Speaking in Germany, Sakakibara said "an excessively strong yen is undesirable, as is an excessively weak yen." \par \par \uc2  By the end of trading the dollar stood at 112.38/43, up modestly from the 112.29/39 open but firmly above Monday's 108.60/65 close. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also closed higher against the Canadian dollar, standing at C$1.5138/48 after opening at C$1.5089/94, but it slipped against most other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro recovered from its recent battering to close at $1.1572/80 after opening at $1.1524/27 and the dollar toppled to 1.3858/68 Swiss francs from 1.3940/50 Swiss francs. The British pound meanwhile rose to $1.6325/30 from $1.6306/11 at the open. \par \par \uc2  As Japan tried to brake the yen's recent run-up, which had forced the dollar nearly six percent lower since the beginning of the year, the United States remained on the sidelines, just as dealers had expected. \par \par \uc2  But Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin did offer some verbal support for the Bank of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  by saying nothing had changed about the Clinton administration's strong dollar policy. He also said the dollar would not be used as a trade tool even amid growing tensions with Japan over steel imports. \par \par \uc2  "There is no reason for the U.S. to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The strong dollar comment might have been a concession," McCarthy said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's gains however did not reflect new found strength and dealers worried in particular about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vulnerability as emerging markets trembled amid signs of a new Latin American crisis. \par \par \uc2  "What we had today was the dollar trading differently against the yen and the euro. It moved off the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on one hand and the Latin America problems on the other," said Rick Gomes, treasurer at Republic National Bank. \par \par \uc2  In Brazil, where a large state recently imposed a debt moratorium and the government is embroiled in a fight about tax hikes, the stock market tumbled over seven percent. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico the peso fell substantially as brokers continued to try and bail out Mexican markets, which slumped amid fears over deepening losses in Brazilian shares. \par \par \uc2  If Latin America continues to look vulnerable in coming sessions, dealers said the attractiveness of the euro from an interest rate differential standpoint would grow against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Australian dollar closed at $0.6368/73, down from $0.6375/80. \par \par \uc2  ((-Svea Herbst-Bayliss, NA Treasury Desk, 212-859-1639 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1c06ofu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
