\par\par \b \uc2  BOND MARKETS-U.S., Europe see gains as gilts wilt. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jeffrey Hodgson \par \uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 1999\par 18:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 12 (Reuters) - U.S. Treasuries and European government bonds saw a session of steady price gains on Tuesday, even as British government debt was battered by a fall in the value of sterling. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasuries rose amid a rally in the dollar against the yen, sparked by reports \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets buying dollars. \par \par \uc2  "Treasuries have got a bit of a bid this afternoon on reports the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen," said Adam Chester, an economist with Halifax Group Treasury in London. \par \par \uc2  "As a consequence of that, and also the slight weakness we're seeing in the equity market at the moment, and the weakness in the Richmond Fed data, the Treasury market is a little bit stronger," he added. \par \par \uc2  The gains in Treasuries on the dollar's rebound began overnight in Asia and extended into the North American session. \par \par \uc2  They followed a session on Monday which saw Treasuries hammered by the slide in the dollar to its lowest levels against the yen in more than two years. The recent slide in the dollar had spurred fears that Japanese investors would begin selling Treasuries and repatriating their money. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. market also benefited on Tuesday on a report from the Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond. The report showed its manufacturing shipments index fell to 4 in December from 8 in November. \par \par \uc2  In Europe, markets were boosted by the rebound in Treasuries as well as bond-friendly German economic data. \par \par \uc2  The German Finance Ministry on Tuesday reported German industrial output fell by 2.3 percent in November, adding the latest to a recent string of downbeat signs on Europe's largest economy. \par \par \uc2  "The industrial production numbers for German were clearly a lot weaker than people had anticipated, which suggests that Q4 for German will be a negative growth quarter. In addition, we have had this sense that the outlook for rate cuts in Europe is still intact," Ifty Islam, global bond strategist with Deutsche Bank. \par \par \uc2  British government bonds, or gilts, took a different path than their U.S. and European counterparts. Gilt prices tumbled as the pound weakened to 4-1/2 month lows against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Gilts have been subject to a bit of profit taking today. They had a very strong run recently on hopes base rates would be cut further, but we have seen sterling coming under pressure recently, and I think international accounts are using that as an opportunity to move into other markets," said Chester. \par \par \uc2  ((Jeffrey Hodgson, International Bonds Unit, +44 171 542 8663, fax +44 171 542 5285, uk.governmentbonds.news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2      This is how major world bond markets looked at 1645 GMT on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday \par \par \uc2  UNITED STATES - \par \par \uc2   Futures: March T-bonds 125-00/32, up 09/32 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab     March Eurodollars 95.005, up 0.025\par \tab     Cash: Long bond at 100-02/32, up 27/32, yield 5.245\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GERMANY -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Futures: March Bunds on Eurex 116.41, up 0.43\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab     March Euromarks 96.910, up 0.010\par \tab     Cash: 10-year Bund 99.88, up 0.34 yield 3.764 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BRITAIN -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Futures: March Long gilts on LIFFE 118.80, down 0.44\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab     March short sterling 94.510, up 0.010\par \tab     Cash: 10-year gilt 136.54, down 0.57 yield 4.357 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ITALY -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Futures: March BTP on LIFFE 114.28, up 0.21\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab     March Eurolire 96.910, up 0.010\par \tab     Cash: 10-year bond (BTP) 104.77, down 0.080, yield\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 3.971 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par JAPAN -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Futures: March JGBs on LIFFE 130.57, up 0.19 from Tok close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab     March Euroyen in Tokyo 99.330, up 0.010.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1c06nvi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
