\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr up on apparent BOJ action, but downside eyed. \b0\par\par\uc2 630 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 1999\par 06:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 12 (Reuters) - The dollar was higher versus the yen by midday on Tuesday after jumping over three yen on apparent dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ has not come to us, but I think they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen starting from below 109 yen through a U.S. financial institution," said a senior trust bank trader. \par \par \uc2  A senior official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  who is in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 111.40/41 yen as of 0321 GMT, compared with 108.60/65 yen in New York late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Tuesday, Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said he was watching movements in the yen closely. \par \par \uc2  "I don't know the cause but I am closely watching recent movements in the yen in Japan and on overseas financial markets," he told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  He declined to comment on the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, saying he left that up to specialists within the ministry. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed that Japanese monetary authorities would not tolerate a fall in the dollar below 110 yen due to the potentially negative economic impact. \par \par \uc2  "I think the BOJ will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again at below 110 yen, and I think they should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Kazuo Takayama chief manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at Midland Bank in Tokyo, said in an interview with Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar buying on Tuesday, the dollar may continue its downward bias against the yen, because traders in Tokyo are pessimistic about the outlook for the U.S. economy, Takayama added. \par \par \uc2  A trust bank dealer said: "The market is still worried about the U.S. economy  and stock market, Brazil and emerging markets, as well as rising trade tensions  between Japan and the U.S." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the dollar to move in a range between 110 yen and 115 yen in the short term. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar rose against the yen as persistent bids from a U.S. financial institution prompted talk that the BOJ was checking on dollar/yen rates. \par \par \uc2  The dollar later extended gains as rumours of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  spread through the market. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes sense when considering the totally out-of-whack dollar bids we were seeing this morning," the second trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  BOJ dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which bankers said may have amounted to as much as $1 billion, pushed the dollar to as high as 111.80 yen from a low of 108.65 yen in Tokyo on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ was likely to have placed dollar bids at several commercial banks that are among eligible agent banks for its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including two major U.S. investment banks, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the euro stood at $1.1483/93 as of 0402 GMT, compared with $1.1507/10  in New York late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The euro stood at 127.70/87 yen compared to 124.89 yen in New York. \par \par \uc2  The euro's sharp rise against the yen was partly due to short-covering spurred indirectly by the dollar's sharp rise versus the yen. \par \par \uc2  A dealer for a Japanese bank said buying from Japanese institutional investors also boosted the euro. \par \par \uc2  Former Japanese Finance Ministry official Makoto Utsumi said on Tuesday the current level of the dollar against the yen was excessive. \par \par \uc2  Utsumi also said: "I don't know what they are thinking, but neither Japan nor the United States can be happy with the dollar below 110 yen." ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 5473 3748 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1c06noh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
