\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Yen bulls revel unchecked. \b0\par\par\uc2 639 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 1999\par 17:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 11 (Reuters) - An ebullient yen leapt to 28-month highs against the dollar on Monday in defiance of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic woes and the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Recent increases in Japanese government bond yields have fuelled speculation that Japanese investors will repatriate money and has helped hoist the yen more than five percent against the dollar since the start of the New Year. \par \par \uc2  Its strength has come at a bad time for the dollar, which in the past week has been saddled with concern that renewed fiscal problems in Brazil will knock the U.S. stock market off its record highs. \par \par \uc2  With concern about capital flows crowding out thoughts of economic fundamentals, traders are expected to drive the yen higher still unless the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acts to halt its gains. \par \par \uc2  "Sentiment towards dollar/yen has turned pretty negative given it has failed to benefit from good economic fundamentals and that Brazilian concerns are lurking in the background," said Nick Stamenkovic, chief European economist at Bank Austria Creditanstalt Futures in London. \par \par \uc2  "As long as fears of Japanese investor repatriation lasts, the dollar will head lower and test 105 (yen)." \par \par \uc2  The dollar has already fallen as low as 108.58 yen, its weakest since September 1996, though it had trimmed its losses to 109.75/85 by 1540 GMT. The yen also advanced as far as 125.83 per euro, its best showing since the new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's launch. \par \par \uc2  The euro's losses against the yen dragged it to its weakest ever against the dollar. It was at $1.1513/18 from a session low of $1.1508 and Friday's late European close of $1.1549/52. \par \par \uc2  The sway that capital flow considerations currently have over the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was highlighted after large sales of dollar/yen by a U.S. fund were said to have sped the dollar towards 108 yen despite wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The train is on its way and dollar/yen is going to work its way lower," said Juergen Lindemann, senior trader at IBJ in London, who expects sustained losses below 108.50 yen to trigger accelerated losses towards 105. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese authorities have so far limited themselves to verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with Vice Finance Minister Koji Tanami warning overnight that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take "appropriate measures" in the event of drastic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market fluctuations. \par \par \uc2  But traders said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to spend money \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to convince the market that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was resolute about halting the yen's rally. \par \par \uc2  The yen's gains helped boost the Australian dollar to 1-1/2 month highs against its U.S. counterpart. A rebound in commodity prices also assisted a rally which lifted it as far as $0.6415, traders said. \par \par \uc2  In Europe, sterling gave a muted response to data showing a worsening in the trend of Britain's manufacturing output and subdued factory gate price pressures. Traders said the data did little more than confirm the outlook for lower British interest rates which has already been discounted by the pound. \par \par \uc2  The weak German industrial orders data also released on Monday could, however, turn out to be damaging for the euro. \par \par \uc2  A decline of 1.5 percent in pan-German industrial orders in November was worse than expected and fanned talk that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could trim rates. While analysts have pencilled in such an easing before the end of the first quarter, a cut has not been fully priced in. \par \par \uc2  "The euro is going to struggle to regain the highs we saw last week given that we have had further signs of economic weakness in Germany," said Stamenkovic at Bank Austria Creditanstalt Futures. \par \par \uc2  ((Swaha Pattanaik, London newsroom, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1b06uho\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
