\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Nervous yen choppy, euro/dlr steady. \b0\par\par\uc2 611 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 1999\par 13:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 8 (Reuters) - The dollar and euro won back ground against the yen by Europe's midsession on Friday, with yen bulls forced to halt by a comment from a Japanese minister warning about the yen's recent strength. \par \par \uc2  Referring to the yen's rise to a 27-month high against the dollar on Thursday, Japan's Economic Planning Agency Minister Taichi Sakaiya told France's La Tribune in an interview that the yen "is certainly at an inappropriate level". \par \par \uc2  Thursday's low of 109.77 yen per dollar meant the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had gained about four percent this week. Dollar/yen was quoted at 111.92/02 at 1135 GMT after gaining nearly one yen from Sakaiya's comment. \par \par \uc2  "The Sakaiya report took the market by surprise and it also came when the market was rather short dollar/yen," said one trader at a Japanese bank in London. "But then I suppose it was natural of him to say that when you consider what's been happening this week." \par \par \uc2  The euro also firmed against the yen, with traders saying this was due to the La Tribune report and not a reflection of sentiment in the new European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen was last at 130.32/52 compared with a session low of 129.43, and up from Thursday's low of 128.00 which was its weakest rate since it first started trading on Monday. \par \par \uc2  During the overnight Asian session the yen had lost ground on talk, later denied by Standard & Poor's and Moody's Investor Service, that an international ratings agency had downgraded Japan's debt. \par \par \uc2  But a dollar/yen rebound was expected to be fairly limited due to factors related to the United States, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "You can't just look at one part of a two-part equation," said Trevor Williams, senior economist at Lloyds. "U.S. interest rates are going lower and there are worries about what might happen in Latin America. If anything goes wrong in Brazil the situation would be very dangerous." \par \par \uc2  Williams was referring to news earlier on Wednesday that Brazil's third-largest state had declared a 90-day moratorium on its debt payments to the central government. On Thursday, Brazil's key Bovespa stock index dropped more than five percent. \par \par \uc2  The market was now awaiting data for the U.S. labour market in December due at 1330 GMT, with the key non-farm payrolls expected to show a rise of 212,000, less than 267,000 the previous month. \par \par \uc2  But while dollar/yen looks sickly, markets will be wary about aggressively assaulting the psychologically crucial 110 level because of fears about Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg said the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not have any bias on interest rates, and that he was happy with the way the euro had moved since Monday. The euro was trading at $1.1651/60 against $1.1676/82 in late Europe on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Nordic \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended their gains against the euro. The Swedish crown gained on speculation about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  joining the euro, while the Norwegian unit was pulled up by its Swedish counterpart and firmer oil prices. \par \par \uc2  "The Swedish and Norway crowns are both now tending to trade as a bloc and Swedish strength is helping Norway," said Michael Metcalfe, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at NatWest Global Financial Markets. "To some extent, both had gone too low towards the end of last year so this strengthening is as much a correction of that fall." \par \par \uc2  ((Chizu Nomiyama, London newsroom 44 171 542 6721, chizu.nomiyama@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv18073fd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
