\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Yen takes breather, euro edges down. \b0\par\par\uc2 696 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 1999\par 10:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 8 (Reuters) - The dollar and euro were trying to find their footing against the yen in European morning trade on Friday after being pulled around by talk, later denied, that Japan's sovereign debt had been downgraded. \par \par \uc2  The euro was generally firm against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , supported by comforting words from European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Wim Duisenberg made late on Thursday, though it had shed some of its earlier gains. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 111.19/29 yen at 0820 GMT, off its overnight high of 112.10 and close to levels seen in late European trade on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen has recovered from the 27-month low of 109.77 which it reached on Thursday amid talk that Japanese investors were repatriating their capital and also non-Japanese investors were showing a growing interest in Tokyo's bond market. \par \par \uc2  But it is still nearly three percent lower than the highs reached early this week, and traders and analysts said the yen's rally over the past few days may have gone too far too fast. \par \par \uc2  "In terms of long-term fundamentals the yen is way overbought, so at some point we should see the yen weaken by quite a long way," said Dick Howard, director of economic research at Julius Baer Investments. \par \par \uc2  "But history has shown that the yen has some prolonged periods of irrationality, so it may be a while (before the yen weakens)," Howard said. \par \par \uc2  Worries about Japan's struggling economy came to the fore to help dollar/yen and euro/yen overnight when talk surfaced that an international ratings agency was downgrading Japan's sovereign or banking sector debt. \par \par \uc2  Standard & Poor's and Moody's both denied they had taken such action. In November, Moody's cut Japan's sovereign debt rating to Aa1 from AAA, citing the nation's deteriorating fiscal stance and inability to pull itself out of recession. \par \par \uc2  While many traders may be itching to test the psychological 110-yen level in dollar/yen again after making a brief assault on it on Thursday, analysts said there would be some wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There is a lot of concern building up among the authorities that a dollar at 110 yen could hurt the economy further and prevent a recovery," said Steve Hannah, director of research at IBJ International. \par \par \uc2  "The main interest of the authorities would be to prevent a rollercoaster situation in which the yen strength snowballs as it goes quickly to 110 and then 100." \par \par \uc2  The euro's moves against the yen mirrored those of dollar/yen. The new European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was last at 130.05/25 yen, up from the low of 128.00 reached on Thursday which was its weakest since its market debut on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Euro/dollar was off its overnight highs but supported by Duisenberg's comment that he was happy with the way the euro has moved since its birth. \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg also said the ECB had no bias in either direction regarding interest rates, which also buoyed the euro. It was last at $1.1663/68, down from $1.1676/82 late on Thursday but up from a low of $1.1550 seen on Wednesday which is its weakest rate so far. \par \par \uc2  "The market wouldn't have been surprised to hear that (Duisenberg's comments)... In any case it is a sensible strategy to maintain stable monetary policy for the euro at the outset," said Hannah at IBJ. \par \par \uc2  There was little impact from data showing German unemployment increased by 34,000 in December on a seasonally adjusted basis, with the unadjusted jobless rate rising to 10.9 percent from 10.2 in November. The German Labour Office said the rise was due largely to seasonal factors. \par \par \uc2  The focus was now on the U.S. labour market data for December, which are due at 1330 GMT today. A Reuters poll of economists forecast non-farm payrolls rising by 212,000, less than an increase of 267,000 in November. \par \par \uc2  ((Chizu Nomiyama, London newsroom 44 171 542 6721, chizu.nomiyama@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1806vn9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
