\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Dlr struggles vs yen, serene vs euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 728 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 1999\par 13:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Jan 6 (Reuters) - The dollar was backtracking against the yen at Europe's midsession on Wednesday, with dollar fans discouraged by the lack of enthusiasm in dollar/yen's rebound from the 27-month low it reached on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  While there was wariness about driving dollar/yen much lower from the viewpoint of economic fundamentals and the danger of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there was also little reason to jump wholeheartedly into the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Supply and demand conditions are pointing firmly towards dollar/yen selling at the moment because Japanese investors want to repatriate their assets ahead of the (financial) year-end," said one trader at a Japanese bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "Even now, there are people waiting to take advantage of any rebound to sell while they can," he added. \par \par \uc2  A key reason for dollar/yen's slide earlier this week, which took it down by 3.5 percent to Tuesday's low of 110.46, was Japanese companies' need to repatriate assets denominated in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for their balance sheets ahead of their financial year-end on March 31. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was quoted at 111.68/78 as of 1145 GMT after rebounding to 112.88 earlier in the day. Its gyrations have also made the euro choppy against the yen since its debut on Monday. \par \par \uc2  So far, euro/yen has moved in a range between 130.00, a low reached on Tuesday, and 135.46 which it hit early on Monday. It was last quoted at 131.36/51. \par \par \uc2  "The yen is the main source of instability at the moment. In that sense it's ironic that the Japanese prime minister is coming to Europe to talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability when the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the one causing instability," said Robin Marshall, chief economist at Chase Investment Bank. \par \par \uc2  Japanese premier Keizo Obuchi starts a tour of Germany, France and Italy on Wednesday to call for closer cooperation on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system. He also hopes to promote the yen so it will not be relegated in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  world after the euro's birth. \par \par \uc2  Amid the bearish sentiment in dollar/yen, the round-figure 110-yen level is becoming both a magnet and an area where the market fears to tread, traders said. \par \par \uc2  While Japan's finance ministry has steered clear of naming specific levels, the number 110 has cropped up in several recent comments from Japan. \par \par \uc2  Japan's former top financial diplomat Makoto Utsumi said a range of 110-120 yen would be comfortable for both the United States and Japan. Sony Corp said it would suffer severely in 1999/2000 if the dollar stayed near 110, heightening fears about the impact of yen strength on Japan's crucial exports industry. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's behaviour once it gets to 110 yen would give a hint as to whether the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the yen's rise, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The market has not entirely dismissed the idea (of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," said Jun Kitazawa, senior corporate trader at DKB in London. "It probably won't happen the moment dollar/yen breaks below 110, but if it slides below that and shows no sign of recovering, then it might happen." \par \par \uc2  While activity centred around the yen, the euro kept its poise against the dollar but slipped against the British pound. Sterling firmness against the dollar and German bank buying of sterling for euros was seen as pushing euro/sterling lower. \par \par \uc2  The euro was last at 70.60/63 pence, off its low of 70.20 but down from 70.96/00 seen in late European trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Euro/dollar was at $1.1751/55 against $1.1770/80 yesterday. The pair has stuck to a range between $1.17 and $1.19 since it began trading on Monday, and traders and analysts said it was unlikely to fluctuate much until the market shed its initial reticence and began to look at economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Marshall at Chase said there were two opposing factors at work, with the dollar pressured by the economic situation in the United States such as the current account deficit and the euro dampened by uncertainty over Europe's policies. \par \par \uc2  ((Chizu Nomiyama, London newsroom 44 171 542 6721, chizu.nomiyama@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv160770b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
