\par\par \b \uc2  G-3/ \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Rates -2: Target Range "May Be In  \highlight22\uc2 Operation \highlight\uc2 " \b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 1998\par 12:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  None of this activity, by itself, amounts to target zones. But Persaud points out that if there were a trading band for the dollar of 15% on either side of what he sees as a reasonable purchasing power parity benchmark of DEM1.60, it would produce precisely the DEM1.35-DEM1.85 range we have seen over most of the past 10 years. \par \par \uc2  "This range may already be in \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he says. \par \par \uc2  Assuming that it isn't, however, the main difference between current official behavior and a G-3 target zone system lies in the apparently shifting goals of G-3 exchange rate management, and in its lack of obvious coordination. Germany, Japan and the U.S. have in the past, and may in the future, pursue opposing goals in the exchange-rate arena. \par \par \uc2  Burke, pointing to recent months' monetary easing by G-3 central banks, believes cooperation is improving. \par \par \uc2  "The message is clear that there is intense coordination and collaboration on the interest-rate front, with one eye on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," Burke said. \par \par \uc2  Evidence for official steering of exchange rates is hardest to find in the U.S. As befits a country whose \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief can send markets into convulsions with phrases like "irrational exuberance" and "oasis of stability," the U.S. abandonment of its strong-dollar policy over the course of the past year has been extremely subtle. It has consisted mainly of U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin declining to repeat his earlier form of words favoring dollar strength, while insisting that policy is unchanged and that he shares Japan's "concern" about the "weak yen." \par \par \uc2  It has included one round of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb dollar strength in June, in which the U.S. spent amounts so small as to do little more than tip its hand to the market. And it has been characterized by an occasional willingness by U.S. government and Federal Reserve officials to find good things to say about the economic impact of a weaker dollar. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 22-12-98 \par \par \uc2  1152GMT \par \par \uc2  1197 4211 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917ducm02hyi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
