\par\par \b \uc2  Sharp euro rise allows policy manoeuvre-ECB Noyer. \b0\par\par\uc2 185 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 1998\par 09:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 8 (Reuters) - A sharp appreciation in the value of the euro would give the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  room for monetary policy manoeuvre, ECB Vice President Christian Noyer told a seminar on Tuesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Noyer said a sharp euro appreciation will have the same effect as a tightening of monetary conditions. \par \par \uc2  "So the logical consequence will be to consider that this (euro appreciation) will give room for manoeuvre on the monetary policy," Noyer said during a question-and-answer session following his speech. \par \par \uc2  Asked what role the yen would play in the ECB's foreign reserve policy, Noyer said the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , along with the dollar, will play a role as one of the bank's main reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Noyer also said in the seminar organised by Paribas that the ECB was currently in the process of finalising various agreements with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the possibility of conducting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on each other's behalf. \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926duc802wlo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
