\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Dlr dive reignites talk of c. bank support. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Andrew Reierson \par \uc2 678 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 1998\par 14:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets delivered a fresh broadside against the dollar on Thursday, plunging it to fresh lows across the board and igniting speculation that central banks could soon step in to smooth market volatility. \par \par \uc2  Confidence in the dollar crumbled amid growing concern about a global recession, prompting increasingly risk-averse international investors into a wholesale exit from the dollar. \par \par \uc2  This exodus has snowballed in the past two days, pushing the dollar below 114 yen, its lowest level since July 1997 and down a startling 16 percent since the start of this week. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fared little better against the mark, sliding to a 20-month low of 1.5870, and against the Swiss franc it tested a 22-month low. \par \par \uc2  A multitude of negative factors was weighing on the dollar. It has been hit by expectations that U.S. interest rates will fall further as a global economic downturn is threatening an economic slowdown in the world's largest economy. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, recent hedge fund losses have exposed the vulnerability of the U.S. financial system. Traders say hedge funds have been a major force behind dollar/yen's slide as they unwind positions. \par \par \uc2  "The de-leveraging of funds, the end of the yen carry trade and Japanese investors paring down losses in U.S. investments are all keeping the pressure on the dollar," said Steve Barrow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bear Stearns in London. \par \par \uc2  The extreme speed of the dollar's collapse has sparked market talk the world's central banks may soon find it necessary to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to smooth chaotic conditions. \par \par \uc2  "There is no fundamental catalyst for any of this move, it's really based on an extinguishing of any risk appetite," said Patrick Bennett, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Warburg Dillon Read in London. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials and politicians said the yen's rise was irregular and too rapid. The speed of the rise and the impact of a much higher yen on exporters knocked Japan's benchmark Nikkei index back 5.78 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. will also be concerned about the excessive volatility and excessive price movement," said Bennett. \par \par \uc2  The aim of the Group of Seven richest nations has been to limit excessive volatility and excessive price movements. \par \par \uc2  Less than four months ago, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. Federal Reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy yen after it slumped to its lowest against the dollar in eight years. \par \par \uc2  In such volatile conditions a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be the lone buyer of dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become a distinct possibility," said one U.S. bank dealer. "Everyone is scared to buy dollars and a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably be the only buyer at this stage." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely only paper over the cracks of deeply bearish dollar sentiment. \par \par \uc2  "Add to that the fact you have credit difficulties with banks tightening their credit stance to investors and other banks and it all adds up to the melting pot of reasons to sell dollars," said Barrow at Bear Stearns. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's extreme moves were evident in the one-week dollar/yen option volatility, which soared to over 40 percent on Thursday to one of its highest levels ever, said option traders. \par \par \uc2  From a chart perspective, the dollar outlook has worsened. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, dollar/yen broke below a 3-1/2 year rising trendline drawn from its all-time low of 79.70 seen in April 1995. This has forced many chartists to consider that the dollar/yen uptrend has finally ended. \par \par \uc2  Against the mark, the chart outlook was bleak for the dollar though it was still holding above a key long-term support line around 1.5790 marks. \par \par \uc2  This is a line on the weekly chart stretching back to dollar/mark's April 1995 lows which, if broken, could also spell the end of the dollar uptrend. \par \par \uc2  ((London newsroom +44 171 542 6745, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113dua801ig1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
