\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Asia markets drop on Wall St, Tokyo steady. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mark Snelling \par \uc2 588 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1998\par 06:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Sept 10 (Reuters) - Asian markets were broadly lower on Thursday after Wall Street fell overnight in the throes of the Clinton sex scandal, but Tokyo was steady after a surprise Japanese credit easing. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei 225 average pared early gains to stand 12.73 points or 0.09 percent lower at 14,742.81 by 0408 GMT, after the first monetary policy change in three years, announced by the Bank of Japan late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The move by the BOJ was a surprise. The downside will become solid following the move, but any gains in shares will be limited as market fundamentals remain weak," said Chisato Haganuma, a strategist at Nomura Securities. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ said its policy making board agreed by majority vote to guide the overnight call rate on average to around 0.25 percent after having kept it close to the official discount rate at 0.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, a dull Australian share market settled lower at midsession after President Bill Clinton's rumbling sex-and-perjury scandal returned to haunt Wall Street. \par \par \uc2  Sydney's benchmark All Ordinaries index slid 18.8 points to 2,523.7, having spent all but the first few minutes of trade meandering in a six point trading band. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Industrial Average earlier closed down 1.94 percent, on profit-taking and hours after the U.S. Congress received another report from independent counsel Kenneth Starr, sparking further talk of a Clinton impeachment. U.S. financial markets were bracing for another volatile session on Thursday as analysts predicted an investor stampede into the relative safety of the U.S. Treasury market. \par \par \uc2  The correction in the ageing U.S. bull market, as well as an overnight slide in the yen hit shares in Hong Kong, where the Hang Seng fell 106 points, or 1.34 percent, to 7,799 in morning trade. \par \par \uc2  "One of the triggers of course is the sudden weakening of the yen which actually puts a little bit of pressure on our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Percy Au-Young, sales director at DBS Securities. \par \par \uc2  "Some people are using that as an excuse to sell but people also still doubt whether this market has truly bottomed out." \par \par \uc2  By mid-morning Tokyo, the dollar was trading around 135 yen from earlier levels above 136 yen, after comments from Japanese finance ministry officials kept \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears afloat. \par \par \uc2  Senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Haruhiko Kuroda said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at an appropriate time if necessary. \par \par \uc2  The weakness in the yen drove the Philippines 30-stock main index through its pyschological support level of 1,100 in early trade, but it recovered slightly to 1106.88, having earlier tumbled 5.4 percent to 1,094.92. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan also had a rough start to the day on Wall Street jitters, dropping 1.32 percent at the open to 6,803.26. \par \par \uc2  And concern over the yen depressed sentiment in Seoul, where the Korea Stock Exchange composite index fell 0.31 of a point to 328.91 by the morning close. \par \par \uc2  In Kuala Lumpur, where shares have been having a slightly better time of it recently, shares opened higher but moved down soon after on profit-taking. \par \par \uc2  The sales were sparked by an Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange announcement that nominees can still sell shares without revealing the names of beneficiaries. \par \par \uc2  The Composite Index was down 0.86 percent at 386.29 by 0202 GMT. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9a00rsv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
