\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dlr Dn On U.S. Rate Cut Speculation \b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1998\par 02:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Speculation that the U.S. may cut interest rates, as well as political uncertainty in the U.S., encouraged dollar selling against the yen and the Deutsche mark, leaving the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower in early Tokyo trading Thursday compared with its levels late in New York Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had risen Wednesday as high as Y138.25 following the decision by the Bank of Japan to ease its monetary stance. Before the decision, it had traded as low as Y130.65 earlier in Wednesday's session. \par \par \uc2  "There are a lot of factors weighing on the dollar," a Japanese city bank trader said. "The Clinton scandal appears to be getting more serious...But another large factor is the possibility that the (U.S.) Federal Reserve may cut interest rates, narrowing the interest rate gap between U.S. and Japan." \par \par \uc2  Concern that U.S. President Clinton has further political difficulties ahead was heightened Wednesday when Independent Prosecutor Kenneth Star delivered to Congress a report on his investigation into Clinton's affair with a former White House intern. \par \par \uc2  Around 0030 GMT (8:30 p.m. EDT), the dollar was trading at Y135.11, down from Y135.35 around 0001 GMT and below Y136.85 in New York late Wednesday. The dollar was quoted at Y132.25 late in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Though the yen has recovered some of its losses against the dollar after the BOJ announcement, Haruhiko Kuroda, the head of the international bureau at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Thursday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the yen as necessary. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also trading at DEM1.7103, lower than DEM1.7109 earlier and below DEM1.7212 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at DEM1.7310 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 10-09-98 \par \par \uc2  0048GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9a07rnk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
