\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar off lows but top-heavy in mid-morning Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1998\par 04:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Sep 3 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2      0206 GMT -- \par \par \uc2      *Dollar came off lows against yen on news that Japanese \par \par \uc2  government has information that North Korea is preparing to \par \par \uc2  launch another missile. \par \par \uc2      *Dollar bounced back after dipping to near 137.20 yen. \par \par \uc2      *But greenback remained top-heavy near 137.60 yen on \par \par \uc2  liquidation and continued sales by overseas fund operators. \par \par \uc2      *Some Japanese exporters seen locking in profits near \par \par \uc2  137.50 yen ahead of first-half book-closing. \par \par \uc2      *Dollar quoted at 137.27/37 yen. \par \par \uc2  *Some Japanese exporters were seen locking in profits near 137.50 yen ahead of first-half book-closings at the end of the month. \par \par \uc2  *Selling accelerated in late morning, with the greenback briefly dipping below 137 yen. \par \par \uc2  *But the dollar lacked active follow-though sales, although another break below 137 yen could send dollar near 136.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  *"More and more dealers are beginning to consider the dollar's downside risk," a dealer at a major city bank said. *Dollar closed at 137.70/80 yen and 1.7485/95 marks in New York on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  0050 GMT - Dollar dipped below 138 yen in early Tokyo on Thursday, pressure by comments from senior officials at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF). \par \par \uc2  *Senior Finance Ministry official Eisuke Sakakibara said on Thursday that excessive yen weakness not yet fully corrected. \par \par \uc2  *Separately, senior Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  at appropriate time if necessary. \par \par \uc2  *"Comments by Sakakibara and Kuroda depressed the dollar, but it was already heavy on the topside after failing to rise above 138.50 yen," a city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  *Sakakibara also said it is risky to have large \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions in current conditions and Japanese investors need to be concerned about holding foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets. \par \par \uc2  *One Japanese bank dealer said a medium-sized Japanese life insurer, who was spotted buying actively in Tokyo on Wednesday, was rumoured to have taken profits this morning. \par \par \uc2  0023 GMT \par \par \uc2  *Dollar well-supported, standing above 138 yen in early Tokyo on Thursday due to short-covering led by interbank operators, but gains limited, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du9302251\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
