\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options: Yen Volatilities Up On  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Jawboning \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1998\par 07:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials sent the dollar down and volatilities implied by yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options up a bit in Tokyo Thursday compared with their levels in New York late Wednesday. Deutsche mark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options are also higher. \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara told reporters early Thursday that the correction to the yen's weakening trend isn't over, while Haruhiko Kuroda, the head of the ministry's international bureau, said the yen should strengthen "much further." \par \par \uc2  After rising to an early intraday high of Y138.42 on sentiment that the U.S. stock market may be stabilizing, the dollar fell through various support levels in the Y137-level to an intraday low of Y136.60 at 0446 GMT (12:46 a.m. EDT). \par \par \uc2  With traders already nervous over the possibility of "event \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " - \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  timed to take advantage a potentially market-moving event - by the BOJ, given Friday's meeting between Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa and U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin, yen volatilities jumped. \par \par \uc2  "With the upcoming meeting and the remarks pushing the dollar down after an earlier rise, bids came in," lifting yen volatilities, a Japanese bank trader said. \par \par \uc2  In the over-the-counter market, one-month at-the-money dollar/yen options imply volatility of 16.8% bid, up from 16.5% in New York Wednesday, but below 17.8% in Tokyo Wednesday. Against the mark, they are higher at 10.5% from 10.2% in New York Wednesday. Dollar/mark options were quoted at 11.2% in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0500 GMT, the dollar was at Y136.70, down from Y137.75, and at DEM1.7425, down from DEM1.7490 late Wednesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Risk-reversals favor dollar put options against the yen, showing the short-term risk for the dollar remains on the downside, dealers said. Risk-reversals measure the market preference for either put or call options by the premium or discount applied. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 03-09-98 \par \par \uc2  0507GMT \par \par \uc2  1077 4127 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9307jim\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
