\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar higher in Tokyo but still seen vulnerable. \b0\par\par\uc2 575 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 1998\par 09:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0600 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     137.63/65\tab \tab 138.00-136.50\par  USD/DEM     1.7502/05\tab \tab 1.7558-1.7465\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  --------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Sept 2 (Reuters) - The dollar was higher against the \par \par \uc2  yen in late afternoon Tokyo on Wednesday on continued \par \par \uc2  short-covering following a sharp overnight recovery in New York \par \par \uc2  stocks. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the dollar's upside remained heavy due to \par \par \uc2  overseas operators' persistent interest in liquidating dollar \par \par \uc2  longs and Japanese investors' hedge-linked selling. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise in late afternoon was led by some overseas operators buying back dollars to lock in profits, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But dollar offers from U.S. fund operators and hedge-linked selling from Japanese investors prevented the greenback from rising above 138 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Today's dollar rise was largely led by short-term specs taking profit on dollar shorts," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  "So the dollar is more likely to test 135 yen again, as it will probably require a lot of time for Wall Street to regain stability," he added. \par \par \uc2  If the dollar slips below 135 yen, the next key support point will be 133.65 yen, the low seen after the U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  joint dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in mid-June, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Situations in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  have not improved and don't justify yen buying," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  "But I think unwinding of yen carry trades by overseas funds will continue, as there are no quick solutions for problems in Russia and other emerging markets." \par \par \uc2  Yen carry trade is a strategy in which fund operators borrow low-cost yen funds and convert them into dollars through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rate swaps. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar rose as high as 138 yen on active follow-through short-covering after a 3.8 percent rise on Wall Street blue-chip stocks. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial posted its second-largest point rise ever on Tuesday, jumping 288.36 points to 7,827.43. \par \par \uc2  Japanese mid-sized life insurers and Asian operators were also rumoured to have bid dollars actively in the morning, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar's direction later was likely to be largely dependent on whether the Dow would continue its rise. \par \par \uc2  "If the Dow rises back above 8,000, speculation of a Fed easing could recede," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  Kyodo news agency quoted Japanese government sources as saying on Tuesday that Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa will likely propose concerted credit easing by the major industrial nations to prevent a global stock meltdown when he meets U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin in San Francisco on Friday. \par \par \uc2  But Eisuke Sakakibara, Japan's top financial diplomat, was quoted as saying by Jiji news agency on Wednesday that the idea of a coordinated interest rate cut by Japan and the United States will not be discussed at this weekend's meeting. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, director-general of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's International Bureau, said on Wednesday that a correction of the excessive strength of the dollar and excessive weakness of the yen has begun. \par \par \uc2  But he also added: "The correction is not yet sufficient." \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at 136.33/43 yen and 1.7505/15 marks in New York on Tuesday. ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du9201zdp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
