\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr steady vs mark, bumpy vs yen, eyes on Russia. \b0\par\par\uc2 622 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 1998\par 13:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 25 (Reuters) - The dollar was generally firmer against the yen in choppy trade on Tuesday, while it barely budged against the mark as the market awaited Russia's plans to restructure its debt. \par \par \uc2  Traders noted that sentiment on the yen was softer after fears faded that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in aid of the yen and amid scepticism about Japanese bank reforms. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 144.55/65 yen at 1035 GMT, off its session high of 144.80 but up from 143.80/90 seen in late European trade on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The news we've had so far today is yen-negative but it seems people are still wary (about driving the yen lower)," said one trader at a Japanese bank in London. "The best way of putting it would be to say that dollar/yen is testing the upper end of its recent range." \par \par \uc2  Yen bears were encouraged when Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said overnight that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  if there was disruption in the market, but added he saw no such disruption right now. In recent days, Japanese officials have often said Tokyo was ready to jump into the market to help the ailing yen. \par \par \uc2  "He's left open the opportunity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the markets are disorderly, but of late that hasn't been the case and verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been sufficient to slow down what looked like a precipitous yen fall," said Eric Fishwick, international economist at Nikko Europe. \par \par \uc2  "But it confirms suspicions the Japanese authorities don't have an implicit exchange rate target," he said. \par \par \uc2  Concerns about the transparency of Japanese bank reforms emerged, meanwhile, when Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi reiterated the authorities would not reveal the results of investigations of individual banks' finances. \par \par \uc2  But Russia was the main focus of attention on Tuesday, with the authorities due to announce later today the terms of converting short-term debt into longer-term paper to make it easier for the government to service. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark had been trapped in a narrow range of about one-third of a pfennig throughout European morning trade as markets awaited Moscow's debt plans. Dollar/mark was at 1.7968/73 against 1.7946/51 in late European trade on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The market was also concerned about New York stocks' performance amid turbulence in Latin American markets. \par \par \uc2  "It's still a bit unclear how the developments (in Russian and Latin American markets) are going to affect the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Glenn Davies, chief economist at Credit Lyonnais Laing. \par \par \uc2  "Potentially, Latin America can have a much bigger impact on the U.S. than Russia can have on Germany...The trade flows are so much bigger between the U.S. and Latin America," he said. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Australian dollar dropped to its lowest in 12 years against the U.S. dollar amid fears that the global market turmoil could lead to further drops in commodities prices. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar was at $0.5765/70, rebounding slightly from its low of $0.5743 although still below $0.5783/88 seen in late Europe. \par \par \uc2  The Nordic \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped to their lowest against the mark since March 1996, with the Swedish crown dragged down by its Norwegian counterpart which in turn was suffering from slumping oil prices. \par \par \uc2  This follows the Norwegian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's declaration on Monday that it would not change interest rates nor \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a "large scale" after raising interest rates by a total of 250 basis points on Friday and Monday to save the crown. \par \par \uc2  ((Chizu Nomiyama, London newsroom 44 171 542 6721, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8p01j5l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
