sn't have a majority in the upper house of parliament, the government will need to compromise to get the bills through. But the opposition could stall their passage by first demanding changes in the government-backed rescue merger plan for troubled Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  If the government is able to pass the bills during the current parliamentary session in time for Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi's U.S. meeting with President Bill Clinton in late September, the yen may benefit. \par \par \uc2  "If (the bills are passed) smoothly during this session of parliament, it would likely boost Japanese stocks, which would also lead to yen buying," said Seiji Masumoto, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Nippon Trust & Banking. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 24-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0613GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8o076nv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
