\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CROSS - Mark sets new high vs Norway,down vs Sfr. \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1998\par 16:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  Swiss franc up vs mark after Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy head Aleksashenko said some Russian banks may fail within days. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Norwegian crown\tab      at 4.3085/05 per mark versus a low at 4.3140 and versus 4.2940/60 per mark late Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  * Analysts said disappointment that Norges bank has not yet raised rates behind Norwegian crown sales, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  over recent weeks not a real solution. \par \par \uc2  * Norwegian deposit rate was raised to 5.5 percent from 5.0 percent on August 11. \par \par \uc2  * Norway crown trade-weighted index at 106.12 vs 105.53 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  * Norway's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it bought a net 426 million crowns between Wednesday and Friday last week. Other data showed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy 1.708 billion crowns between August 10 and 11. \par \par \uc2  * Mark off new four-week lows against yen as profit-taking set in motion last week continues, Russian bank failure news adds to seeling pressure. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Mark slides to session lows at 83.54/57 Swiss centimes\tab      down from Thurs high at 83.97 centimes and versus 83.77/80 centimes in late Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Bundesbank leaves interest rates unchanged, sets next two weekly securities repurchase tenders at an unchanged fixed rate of 3.30 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * German July annualised M3 grows five percent from fourth quarter 1997 against 5.3 percent in June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Mark/yen\tab      at 79.03/06 versus 79.97/80.00 in late Europe trade on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Fears of Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and profit-taking on short positions continue to underpin yen. Dlr/yen sinks to new 3-wk low.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Japanese officials in recent days have warned of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the most recent warning issued Thursday by chief of the Finance Ministry's International Bureau, Haruhiko Kuroda.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * German foreign minister Klaus Kinkel warns against too much Russia gloom. Earlier this week, Russia effectively devalued the rouble and announced a 90-day moratorium on some foreign debt repayments.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Sweden's Riksbank leaves repo rate unch at 4.10 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Mark/Swedish crown\tab      at 4.5205/35 against early high at 4.5400 and versus 4.5420/50 on Weds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Pratima Desai, London newsroom +44 171 542 2737)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8k01amg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
