\par\par \b \uc2  Yen holds gains against majors at Europe midday. \b0\par\par\uc2 596 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1998\par 13:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 20 (Reuters) - The yen stuck close to its three-week highs against the dollar and mark at Europe's midsession as traders continued to mull the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  While there have been no signs of the Bank of Japan buying yen for dollars amid dollar/yen's fall of more than three percent so far this week, the market was edgy. \par \par \uc2  "In the very short run, any sort of talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or fear of it in the background will certainly support the yen," said Ian Morris, international economist at HSBC James Capel. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 142.66/71 yen at 1045 GMT, off its three-week low of 142.30 but down from 144.20/25 seen in late European trade on Wednesday. This is a drop of nearly four percent from the eight-year high of 147.63 seen earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  Mark/yen suffered similarly, struggling near its three-week low at 79.48/52 yen against 79.97/00 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The chief of the Japanese Finance Ministry's International Bureau, Haruhiko Kuroda, was the latest of a series of top-level Japanese officials to warn the markets about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Kuroda said that while the dollar/yen's trend had changed a bit, the yen needs to rise further, and that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the appropriate time as necessary. \par \par \uc2  "Obviously the market remembers what happened back in June (when the Federal Reserve and BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), when they moved it quite sharply even though it was for the short term," said Glenn Davies, chief economist at Credit Lyonnais Laing. \par \par \uc2  "Probably there are traders taking the view that if there is going to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they might as well wait for that before shorting the yen again," Davies added. \par \par \uc2  Analysts were doubtful about the yen-boosting effect of any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying U.S. and Japanese fundamentals would soon undermine the yen again. \par \par \uc2  "In the U.S. we are now in post-GM-strike mode and we will soon get bouncebacks in economic data," said Morris at HSBC, referring to a strike at General Motors. "We also have a tightening bias by the Fed, and even though they probably won't raise rates, it's probably enough to provide support for the dollar." \par \par \uc2  Against the mark, the dollar was trapped in a range of less than one pfennig, and was quoted at 1.7942/52 against late Wednesday's 1.7969/79. \par \par \uc2  The German Bundesbank, following its first council meeting after its summer break, decided on Thursday to leave interest rates unchanged, as the market expected. \par \par \uc2  The focus, as far as the mark was concerned, was on events unfolding in Russia where the authorities delayed until Monday their debt restructuring announcement, which had originally been due on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "It's certainly one of the main factors...On Monday, Russia will announce its debt rescheduling and that will be a contributory factor for the mark in the days ahead," said Gianpaolo Mosconi, analyst at Sanwa. \par \par \uc2  The British pound was firm although off its session highs, bolstered by stronger-than-expected growth in UK money supply which grew by 1.5 percent on the month in July compared with forecasts of 0.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  Sterling/mark was at 2.9200/05 against 2.9191/96 in late Europe on Wednesday, and sterling/dollar was at $1.6280/88 against $1.6228/38. \par \par \uc2  ((Chizu Nomiyama, London newsroom 44 171 542 6721, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8k018ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
