\par\par \b \uc2  Yen fights back, backed up by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears. \b0\par\par\uc2 596 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1998\par 10:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 20 (Reuters) - The yen gained ground in Europe to rise to a three-week high against the dollar and mark, with yen bears holding back amid fears the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in aid of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It's got more to do with what the market's anticipating... Sometimes talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be more effective than the actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself," said Gianpaolo Mosconi, analyst at Sanwa in London. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 142.35/43 yen at 0740 GMT, just off its low and down from 144.20/25 seen in late European trade on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The mark was at its lowest since July 28 at 79.41/44 yen, falling from 79.97/00 seen in late European dealings on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Various top-level Japanese officials have warned of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days, with the chief of the Japanese Finance Ministry's International Bureau, Haruhiko Kuroda, issuing the most recent of these on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda said while the dollar/yen's trend has changed a bit, the yen needs to rise further, and that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the appropriate time as necessary. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the impact of yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would depend on the circumstances at the time. \par \par \uc2  "Mr Miyazawa recognises that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be a waste of time without fundamental initiatives in banking reforms and fiscal stimulus," said Paul Chertkow, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  But Chertkow noted that current market conditions might be suitable for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying: "The possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is mounting, given that short cash positions have been turned and given the dollar-put options positions in the market." \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market would be nervous ahead of key events for Japan in early September. Chinese President Jiang Zemin - whose own economy has suffered due to the yen's weakness - visits Japan, and Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa will travel to the United States around the same time. \par \par \uc2  The falls in dollar/yen and mark/yen were keeping dollar/mark in a tight range, but its tone was soft in line with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's drop against other majors. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark was quoted at 1.7927/32, near its session low, against 1.7969/79 in late Europe on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the German Bundesbank holds its first council meeting after its summer break, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it would not hold a news conference afterwards and the market expects interest rates to stay on hold. \par \par \uc2  Rather, the focus was on developments in Russia after Moscow delayed until Monday its debt restructuring announcement, which had originally been due on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "It's certainly one of the main factors...On Monday, Russia will announce its debt rescheduling, and that will be a contributory factor for the mark in the days ahead," said Mosconi at Sanwa. \par \par \uc2  The British pound, meanwhile, edged up slightly after data showing UK M4 money supply increased more than expected in July, rising by 1.5 percent on the month compared with forecasts of 0.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  The market shrugged off data showing British second-quarter GDP grew by an unrevised rate of 0.5 percent from the previous quarter, which was in line with economists' forecasts. \par \par \uc2  Sterling/mark was quoted at 2.9150/55 against 2.9191/96 in late Europe on Wednesday, and sterling/dollar at $1.6257/67 against $1.6228/38. \par \par \uc2  ((Chizu Nomiyama, London newsroom 44 171 542 6721, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8k01811\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
