\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar edges lower vs yen in afternoon Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1998\par 07:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Aug 20 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2      0445 GMT --*Dollar dipped below 143.50 yen in early \par \par \uc2  afternoon trade on options-related stop-loss sales and yen \par \par \uc2  buying in cross trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      *Further stop-loss dollar sales expected at 143.00 yen, \par \par \uc2  although some buying by Japanese operators expected at lower \par \par \uc2  end of 143-144 yen. Dollar quoted at 143.30/40 yen. \par \par \uc2      *A dealer at a European bank said dollar still in \par \par \uc2  corrective phase versus yen and operators remain keen to buy \par \par \uc2  yen for hedging, particularly against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      *He sees dollar's near-term bottom at 142.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  *"Operators are lagging behind in hedge sales of marks and other cross \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and those sales are likely to put downward pressure on dollar/yen rate," said the dealer. \par \par \uc2  *Speculative dollar sales that pushed it down below 143.50 yen was partly driven by earlier remarks by senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Haruhiko Kuroda, said a bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  *Kuroda said on Thursday that dollar/yen trend has changed a bit but that yen needs to appreciate further. \par \par \uc2  *In brief remarks to reporters, Kuroda, head of the ministry's International Bureau, also said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at the appropriate time as necessary. \par \par \uc2  0300 GMT \par \par \uc2  *Dollar softer against yen on fears of possible yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but was supported on buying interest from Japanese investors, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *Disappointment that public funds may not be injected to support Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan Ltd  and falling Tokyo stocks also underpinned the greenback, they said. \par \par \uc2  *"The dollar is still on a downward bias due to strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears, but taking it lower will be difficult unless fresh incentives materialise," a dealer at a Japanese commercial bank said. \par \par \uc2  *Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi and Bank of Japan on Thursday denied another newspaper report that government was considering using public funds to facilitate merger between the troubled LTCB and Sumitomo Trust and Banking Co Ltd. \par \par \uc2  *Nihon Keizai Shimbum reported on Thursday that the government was mulling measures, including injecting between 500 billion yen and one trillion yen into LTCB. \par \par \uc2  *"There is no truth in what was reported," said a senior BOJ official, but he added the bank would continue to closely monitor developments in their merger talks. \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-1396 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8k017g8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
