\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar softer versus yen but stuck by midday Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2 463 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1998\par 06:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0300 GMT\tab      TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0300 GMT\par  USD/JPY     143.90/93\tab \tab    144.20-143.55\par  USD/DEM     1.7957/60\tab \tab    1.7988-1.7955\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  --------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Aug 20 (Reuters) - The dollar was softer against the \par \par \uc2  yen on fears of possible yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but was \par \par \uc2  supported on buying interest from Japanese investors, dealers \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  Disappointment that public funds may not be injected to \par \par \uc2  support Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan Ltd  and falling \par \par \uc2  Tokyo stocks also underpinned the greenback, they said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is still on a downward bias due to strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears, but taking it lower will be difficult unless fresh incentives materialise," a dealer at a Japanese commercial bank said. \par \par \uc2  Steady buying by Japanese importers and investors on dips provided support, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There are still players who couldn't buy (dollars) before the recent rally, which is capping the yen's rise," a dealer at a trust bank said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's downside firmed on bids aimed at protecting options-related orders at 143.50 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi and the Bank of Japan on Thursday denied another newspaper report that the government was considering using public funds to facilitate a merger between the troubled LTCB and Sumitomo Trust and Banking Co Ltd. \par \par \uc2  "There is no truth to such reports," Obuchi said in response to a question in the budget committee of parliament's Upper House. The Nihon Keizai Shimbum reported on Thursday that the government was mulling measures, including injecting between 500 billion yen and one trillion yen into LTCB. \par \par \uc2  "There is no truth in what was reported," said a senior BOJ official, but he added the bank would continue to closely monitor developments in their merger talks. \par \par \uc2  An LTCB spokesman declined to comment on the report. \par \par \uc2  Falling Tokyo stock prices also buoyed the dollar. The key Nikkei 225 average was down 81.51 points at 15,324.83 as of 0401 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Commercial demand at the 0100 GMT fixing partly lifted the dollar above 144 yen in mid-morning Tokyo but the greenback was unable to sustain gains on sales by U.S. fund operators, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  There was short-covering demand on dips, as positions were leaning short following the recent downward trend. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, further verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by monetary authorities should keep the dollar top-heavy, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Haruhiko Kuroda said on Thursday that the yen's fall has not corrected enough, although the dollar/yen trend has changed a bit. \par \par \uc2  He also told reporters that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at the appropriate time as necessary. ((Tamawa Kadoya, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8k0170l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
