\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar tumbles over one yen on overseas funds. \b0\par\par\uc2 585 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1998\par 09:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0611 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     142.80/90\tab \tab 144.20-142.55\par  USD/DEM     1.7934/44\tab \tab 1.7928-1.7988\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  --------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Aug 20 (Reuters) - The dollar sank more than one yen \par \par \uc2  by late trade on Thursday, with lingering caution over \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and aggressive sales by overseas funds knocking \par \par \uc2  the dollar below 143 yen for the first time since July 30. \par \par \uc2  "Sales by overseas funds were so aggressive and persistent \par \par \uc2  that traders here got confused with them. But those sales may \par \par \uc2  lead to a further fall of the dollar," said one bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  A senior trader at a European bank said dollar sales by overseas funds were aimed at fixing profits in dollar/yen positions before a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Since Japanese operators were overwhelmed by overseas operator sales and were refraining from placing firm bids on falls, the dollar's downside risks are growing," he added. \par \par \uc2  Senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Haruhiko Kuroda said on Thursday that dollar/yen trend has changed a bit but that yen needs to appreciate further. In brief remarks to reporters, Kuroda also said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at the appropriate time as necessary. \par \par \uc2  The dealer at the European bank said the dollar's voluntary correction against the recent rally to 147.64 yen may send the dollar down below 140 yen. \par \par \uc2  But even if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place, the greenback could be supported at around 135-138 yen, he added. \par \par \uc2  Some traders speculated that active dollar sales by U.S. funds might be due to expectations that the Japanese government may hammer out new measures to bail out ailing Japanese banks. \par \par \uc2  The Nihon Keizai Shimbum said on Thursday the government was mulling measures, including injecting between 500 billion yen and one trillion yen into Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi and the Bank of Japan on Thursday denied the newspaper report that the government was considering using public funds to facilitate a merger between the troubled LTCB and Sumitomo Trust and Banking Co Ltd. \par \par \uc2  "There is no truth to such reports," Obuchi said in response to a question in the budget committee of parliament's Upper House. \par \par \uc2  But government sources told Reuters that the idea of using public funds before the merger is under discussion, but analysts said there is great uncertainty over whether such plans would be approved by parliament. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at another European bank said the dollar is in a corrective phase versus the yen and many operators remained keen to buy the yen for hedging, particularly against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the mark. \par \par \uc2  "Operators are lagging behind in hedge sales of marks and other cross \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and those sales are likely to put downward pressure on the dollar/yen rate," said the dealer. \par \par \uc2  The mark was quoted at 79.66/69 yen at 0705 GMT against 80.12 yen in late New York trade on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  He said yen buying also took place against the Swiss franc and the Australian dollar. \par \par \uc2  Japanese players were still bullish on the dollar on a medium-to long-term basis and were loath to buy the yen with conviction amid the sluggish economy, said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 144.02/12 yen and 1.7980/85 marks in New York on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Tatsuo Ito, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-1396 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8k0168s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
