\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Crisis/Glance:Japan Indicators Below 50.0 For Ninth Mo \b0\par\par\uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1998\par 11:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  -- Japan's index of leading economic indicators in June stood at 30.0, the ninth straight month below the boom-or-bust threshold of 50.0. \par \par \uc2  -- Japan's economy has suffered declines in some prices, but the economy is not in a deflationary spiral and policymakers don't need to make policies that would drive prices higher, said Sakaiya, director-general of the EPA. \par \par \uc2  -- Japan posted a merchandise trade surplus of Y1.316 trillion in July, up 56.8% from the year-earlier month \par \par \uc2  -- As speculation of the future of the Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan continued President Obuchi denied local media reports that the government plans to lend assistance to the bank. \par \par \uc2  The head of the agency inspecting the LTCB met with the president of Sumitomo Trust & Banking in a bid to spur the merger of the two banks, Nikkei News reported. \par \par \uc2  The top bureaucrat at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it is possible that the situation surrounding the troubled bank could well affect the overall financial system. \par \par \uc2  -- The head of the international bureau at \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  Kuroda says \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  appropriately as needed in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, but won't comment on the timing of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -- The Hong Kong government continued buying blue-chip shares pushing the Hang Seng Index higher. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's quasi-\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to maintain its pressure on speculators for a long time, a local newspaper reported. \par \par \uc2  Yam, the head of the HKMA, called on G-7 economies to rethink their stance on non-\b \highlight22\uc2 interventionism\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -- Hong Kong's chief executive Tung said the territory's gross domestic product shrank in the second quarter ended June 30, while the third and fourth quarters will be "very difficult." \par \par \uc2  -- Malaysian Shares rose sharply early in the day with the KLSE Comp Index gaining 7.3% by midday, but profit-taking in the afternoon saw that dip to end only 2.2% up. Much of the buying was speculative on the back of government comments of the possibilities of market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -- Market players bought back the yen against the dollar in Tokyo to square short positions amid heightened concern about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; at 0810 GMT, the U.S. dollar is at Y142.66, down from Y144.07, and at DEM1.7926, down from DEM1.1.7977 late Wednesday in New York \par \par \uc2  -- Tokyo stocks end marginally lower, with the Nikkei down 14.93 at 15,391.41 [5011] \par \par \uc2  -- The Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi is to dispose of around Y400 billion bad loans in the current fiscal year, up from Y270 billion it was to originally write off, said a major Japanese daily. \par \par \uc2  -- The value of Japan's energy imports in July dropped 14.5% to Y489.96 billion from July 1997, according to merchandise trade balance statistics. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0941GMT \par \par \uc2  1042 4190 55126 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8k073ck\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
