\par\par \b \uc2  China Can Keep Yuan Stable Despite Devalued Ruble - Report \b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1998\par 08:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BEIJING (Dow Jones)--China can maintain a stable yuan exchange rate despite the ruble's recent devaluation, China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  newspaper, the Financial News, said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  China doesn't suffer from the same economic woes that forced Russia to devalue the ruble, the newspaper said. \par \par \uc2  The report attributed the ruble's devaluation to weakness in the Russian economy and problems in its political system and society. \par \par \uc2  It also said that Russia's financial crisis was partly influenced by Southeast Asia's economic turmoil and the "manipulation" of international speculators. \par \par \uc2  In contrast, the report said, China's restricted capital markets and limited yuan convertibility prevent speculators from attacking its economy. \par \par \uc2  "But the influence of the Asian financial crisis on China's exports should not be underestimated," the report added. \par \par \uc2  Japan is in a "key position" to cause global economic turmoil, it said. "A sharp drop in the yen can cause more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluations around the world." \par \par \uc2  The newspaper urged the U.S. and European countries to cooperate with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to conduct joint \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if the yen continues to drop. \par \par \uc2  It also urged Japan to implement more active policies to stimulate its economy. \par \par \uc2  Continued weakness in the yen, the recent devaluation of the ruble and China's own slowing economy have raised fears that China will devalue the yuan to boost economic growth. \par \par \uc2  However, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said recently a devaluation won't boost exports because over half of China's exports rely on imported materials that would become more expensive after a yuan depreciation. \par \par \uc2  China's yuan can only be converted under the current account for trade-related purposes, so a decision to devalue could only be made by the government. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Russia cut Monday the lower limit for the ruble (RUR) by 34% to RUR9.50 to the dollar, from RUR6.30 to the dollar previously. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0658GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8k0731x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
