\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup: Dlr Lower; Mkt Braces For  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Arran Scott \par \uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1998\par 07:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Market players bought back the yen against the dollar and the mark in Tokyo Thursday in order to square short positions amid heightened concern about potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended Asian trading lower against both the yen and the Deutsche mark compared with its levels in New York late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Escalating verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese monetary authorities has put \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders on guard, creating a situation in which even those who don't believe \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely are scurrying to liquidate long-dollar positions in a defensive action. \par \par \uc2  "We'd like to be well prepared for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That means either squaring dollar long positions (against the yen) or taking short-dollar positions," said Tatsuya Ishii, senior sales manager and head of customer \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Banque Nationale de Paris in Tokyo. "At the moment, the dollar's downside risk is greater than the upside." \par \par \uc2  The latest dose of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came Thursday from Haruhiko Kuroda, the head of the international bureau at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , who warned that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as necessary. \par \par \uc2  "The excessively strong dollar and weak yen are far from being corrected. It's still necessary for this to be corrected," Kuroda said, adding, "We will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  appropriately as necessary." \par \par \uc2  Kuroda's comments had little impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, but they added to the darkening sentiment enveloping the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0530 GMT (1:30 a.m. EDT), the dollar is quoted at Y143.09, below Y144.07 late Wednesday in New York and down from Y144.25 late Wednesday in London. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also is at DEM1.7942, lower than DEM1.7977 late Wednesday in New York and below DEM1.7975 in London Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 20-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0559GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 28038 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8k072tl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
