\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo -2: Mkt Awaits Release Of FOMC Minutes \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1998\par 02:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The mark is trading at Y80.00, up from Y79.95 earlier but below Y80.14 in New York late Wednesday. The mark was quoted late in Tokyo Wednesday at Y80.26. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6233, up from $1.6223 earlier but below $1.6235 in New York late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.6168 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is seen trading between Y143.30-Y144.50 and DEM1.7930-DEM1.8050 for the rest of the Asian day. \par \par \uc2  Despite worries about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the city bank dealer said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to take action until after Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa's meeting with Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin, slated for Sept. 4-5. \par \par \uc2  "The top people have to agree before any action is taken," he said. \par \par \uc2  In addition to jitters about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , speculation that U.S. hedge funds are selling the dollar for yen to book profits to offset losses incurred from investment in Russia and other emerging markets are lending support to the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  What's more, participants are closing out long mark positions against the yen amid anxiety over Russia's economic turmoil, lending further support to the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Japan's trade data for July released earlier Thursday was within the market's expectations and had little impact on dollar-yen trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's merchandise trade surplus rose 56.8% in July from a year earlier to Y1.316 trillion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. Japan's politically sensitive trade surplus with the U.S. rose 59.7% to Y669.72 billion. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Looking ahead, market players will closely watch the release later in\par the day of the Federal Open Market Committee minutes, said the second\par city bank dealer.\par By Sonoko Setaishi 813-5255-2933; ssetaishi@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0059GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (CORRECTED 0221GMT)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8k0724q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
