x finished higher, rising 119.95\par points to 7742.53.\par    --Tokyo stocks ended lower, with the Nikkei down 14.93\par at 15,391.41.\par    --Japan's index of leading economic indicators in June\par stood at 30.0, the ninth straight month it was below the\par boom-or-bust threshold of 50.0.\par    --Japan's economy has suffered declines in some prices,\par but the economy isn't in a deflationary spiral and\par policymakers don't need to make policies that would drive\par prices higher, said Taichi Sakaiya, director-general of the\par Economic Planning Agency.\par    --Amid speculation about the future of the Long-Term\par Credit Bank of Japan, Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi denied\par local media reports that the government plans to lend\par assistance to the bank.\par    --The top bureaucrat at Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 ministry of finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Koji\par Tanami said it is possible that the situation surrounding\par the troubled LTCB could well affect the overall financial\par system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-20-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0921EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1141 4223 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8k021wr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
