\par\par \b \uc2  World Mkt Turmoil At A Glance:Russia Ctrl Bk Plans Guarantee \b0\par\par\uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1998\par 13:00\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --Seeking to prevent a run on the Russian banking system,\par Russia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it is planning a 100% guarantee on\par all individual deposits at the country's commercial banks.\par    --Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  shot higher against the U.S.\par dollar during Asian trading, propelled by a surge in the\par value of the yen.\par    --The head of the international bureau at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 ministry of finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Haruhiko Kuroda said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par appropriately as needed in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, but\par wouldn't comment on the timing of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --The dollar was lower against the yen in midmorning\par London trade amid concerns that Japanese authorities are\par preparing to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the yen. The dollar was\par trading at Y142.73, down from Y143.09 at 0530 GMT in Tokyo\par and Y144.07 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was also\par at DEM1.7924, down from DEM1.7942 in Tokyo and DEM1.7977 in\par New York.\par    --Gerhard Schroeder, the Social Democratic Party's\par candidate for German chancellor, expressed worries about the\par influence the financial crises in Asia and Russia could have\par on European growth.\par    --U.S. Treasurys were lower at midmorning in London,\par reacting to the declining dollar. The benchmark 30-year bond\par was at 98 27/32, down 11/32, to yield 5.58%.\par    --The Hang Seng Index finished higher, rising 119.95\par points to 7742.53.\par    --Tokyo stocks ended lower, with the Nikkei down 14.93 at\par 15,391.41.\par    --Japan's index of leading economic indicators in June\par stood at 30.0, the ninth straight month it was below the\par boom-or-bust threshold of 50.0.\par    --Japan's economy has suffered declines in some prices,\par but the economy isn't in a deflationary spiral and\par policymakers don't need to make policies that would drive\par prices higher, said Taichi Sakaiya, director-general of the\par Economic Planning Agency.\par    --Amid speculation about the future of the Long-Term\par Credit Bank of Japan, Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi denied\par local media reports that the government plans to lend\par assistance to the bank.\par    --The top bureaucrat at Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 ministry of finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Koji\par Tanami said it is possible that the situation surrounding the\par troubled LTCB could well affect the overall financial system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-20-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0700EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1141 4223 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8k021rw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
