\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE -  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  threat buoys yen bulls. \b0\par\par\uc2 621 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1998\par 18:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 19 (Reuters) - The yen bulls gained the upper hand in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Wednesday, gathering strength from an ongoing stream of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Japanese officials to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar eased to a fresh two-week low against the yen, the mark slipped to a three-week low and sterling was pushed to its lowest against the Japanese unit since late July. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said yen gains have been halting in thin, nervous trade as the market weighed up the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the ongoing bleak outlook for the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think we'll see \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon, the Japanese authorities have already done an excellent job in talking the momentum out of the market," said a U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers are finding the authorities' \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  warnings hard to ignore and are erring on the side of caution, trimming back short yen positions. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Vice Finance Minister Eisuke Sakakibara added to the past few days' \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rhetoric with an explicit warning overnight that the risks of a stronger yen were growing and the chances of yen supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  drawing nearer. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen responded by distancing itself even further from last week's eight year highs above 147, slipping back to 143.86/96 in late European trade and well below late Tuesday's European level of 144.83/88 yen. \par \par \uc2  Mark/yen behaved in similar fashion, dipping down to levels around 79.80 yen before recovering to 80.00/03 in late trade. It stood at 80.55/58 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  But most analysts see the yen losing its new-found composure, arguing the market has girded itself for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action and thus has already cushioned the impact if it comes. \par \par \uc2  "The last round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June showed perfect timing and caught the market long of dollars," said Jesper Dannesboe, treasury economist at ABN-Amro in London. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar/yen option risk reversal is favouring yen calls which indicates dollar/yen may not be that vulnerable to the downside if there is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The option risk reversal measures the price of a call option against its relative put which can indicate the market's bias. \par \par \uc2  This demand for yen calls suggests the market is preparing for a stronger yen, unlike the June \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the market was caught favouring yen puts, or further yen losses. \par \par \uc2  Dennesboe is also wary of chart support at 143.50 and long-term trend support in the 142 yen area which could provide a strong base for dollar bulls. \par \par \uc2  Dealers also have to weigh up Japan's weak economic outlook, which is seen eventually exerting fresh pressure on the yen. \par \par \uc2  "This won't be a big turnaround for the yen. For that to happen, we need stronger data out of Japan and Japanese assets need to become more attractive," said Klaus Kusber, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson in Frankfurt. \par \par \uc2  "And I think it's a bit early for that, though we should see better economic data towards the end of the year." \par \par \uc2  The market is set to contend with another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Sakakibara attends a private financial seminar in Aspen, Colorado later on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, dollar/mark stuck to a narrow orbit around 1.80 marks. With the volatility from Russian markets abating and little on the U.S. data front for the rest of this week, dealers see the current calm continuing for now. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 1.7977/87 marks compared with 1.7979/84 marks seen late Tuesday in Europe. \par \par \uc2  ((Andrew Reierson, London newsroom +44 171 542 6745, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8j014vw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
